  "description": "Audit-write fidelity (PR #1111 / Obs-Meta + Trace-IDs Mega-PR, 5ead9b7cd). Four panels cover the two new counters from PR #1111 C2 (`<daemon>_audit_log_write_total{endpoint,kind}` and `<daemon>_audit_log_write_failures_total{endpoint,kind,error_class}` — per-daemon prefix, pre-instantiation grid at pkg/wire/metrics.go:3142-3179). The audit emit is best-effort by design (ADR-035): the user-facing action has already returned 200 to the customer by the time AppendEvent runs, so a failed insert logs WARN and bumps the counter without rolling back. A sustained non-zero rate therefore means audit rows are silently missing while customer traffic looks healthy — a ticket-tier operational signal, not a page-tier outage. Cross-daemon queries use `{__name__=~`.+_audit_log_write_total`}` because the metric prefix is per-daemon; the dashboard covers apid + schedd + meterd + gatewayd-internal (the auditEndpointClosedSet at pkg/wire/metrics.go:3097). Companion alert: FaasAuditWriteFailuresSpike (warn, cross-daemon, family=audit_write, component=platform — deliberately NOT paired with the apid-only FaasApidAuditWriteFailures so non-apid spikes stay visible). Runbook: docs/runbooks/FaasAuditWriteFailuresSpike.md.",
  "editable": true,
  "fiscalYearStartMonth": 0,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "id": null,
  "links": [],
  "liveNow": false,
  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Audit writes / 5m by endpoint",
      "description": "Stacked time series of all audit-write successes across the auditEndpointClosedSet (apid / schedd / meterd / gatewayd-internal) over the rolling 5m window. Cross-daemon regex matches every `<daemon>_audit_log_write_total` series; the `endpoint` label is set independently by `pkg/audit.audit.go:296` (a.actor).",
      "id": 1,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (endpoint) (rate({__name__=~\".*_audit_log_write_total\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{endpoint}}",
          "refId": "A"
